//@version=6
indicator("GTOP Butterfly Tool", shorttitle="GTOP Butterfly", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=250, behind_chart=false)

// Candidate 2026-10-15: shared GTOP rulebook 1.3.0. See docs/GTOP_ALIGNMENT.md.
// Boundary closes remain pending; higher-timeframe follow-through uses its own close.
// Model 1 selections require the assigned timeframe and a local body purge to verify.
// H4 modes: GTOP 1/5/9 default, explicit NY windows, alignment notice, optional Chart H4.
// INSTALL: Update the separate Test 2 / GTOP Butterfly Tool, never the original v2.5.
// Separate fixed-box test variant of the saved v2.5 source; do not overwrite it.
// Automatic and gray context boxes use their original source start/end times.
// Source bounds are preserved; shared qualification/confirmation rules govern state.
// H1 shift-hour admission is independent: relevant parents can coexist.
// Confirmed Daily/Weekly endpoints are processed immediately, without waiting
// for the next source bar; developing bars never qualify this shortcut.
// Forming Monthly/Daily/Weekly observations use confirmed parent candidates and complete
// offered main-source H/L/close; the existing true-realtime endpoint fallback
// remains available for gaps. Ordinary source prices never classify formation.
// They never advance closed-candle variants or persistent state.
// Automatic ranges show title + variant; hover any range title for full details.
// Compact titles stay on the known purge side, anchored to the original source candle.
// 2026-10-12 Rex: extended captions point to the high/low being purged.
// Outward layout separates estimated title footprints and reserves source anchors.
// Dotted black connectors link crowded titles to their source-box edges.
// 2026-10-13 Rex: dotted caption connectors without arrowheads.
// 2026-10-13 Rex: label extenders, source-edge accents and DOL lines default to black.
// Pine cannot measure screen-pixel bounds,
// so extreme zoom/density can still overlap. Actual DOL endpoints carry an eye.
// Current-only geometry, date and optional archives follow the latest available MAIN head.
// No chart-visible-time dependencies: panning does not request recalculation.
// Parent status follows Replay-mapped source data independently of panning.
// Parent collection requests execute only at main historical/live endpoints.
// Pending DOL lines cover the source boundary and reach the available observation time.
// BASELINE ONLY, 2026-10-13: native TradingView compilation and live NAS100 M5/H1 rendering
// verified. XAUUSD M5 also verified, including retained H1 shift CRTs with
// History enabled and the H1 parent selected. Latest dotted/black styling installed.
// Intraday Bar Replay remains outside the verified scope; unavailable assigned
// evidence is explicitly unverified. Live rendering is not a signal-accuracy claim.
// Scheduled ranges develop only inside their own window, then freeze.
// Separate Butterfly script: preserve the original v2.5 and personal drawings.
// v2.5 UI candidate: qualified Butterfly context by default; H1-and-lower time ribbon.
// Relevant = one side purged + own-timeframe close back inside + pending DOL.
// All layers advance chronologically; forming copies never confirm a source.
// Keep a relevant range until delivery/invalidation, then advance to the next
// qualifying range. The watermark sticky note never drives selection.
// This visual aid does not confirm an entry. See README for confirmation timing.
// The compact chart drawing is retained: a slim, light time-aligned strip
// inside the PRICE chart. Its blocks use real New York timestamps and move
// with candles when scrolling/zooming. The ribbon uses no fixed-screen table
// or separate pane; only the watermark/note remains pinned to chart corners.
// If updating a pane-based version, remove/re-add this chart instance so the
// overlay setting takes effect. Existing manual chart drawings are untouched.
// Ribbon vertical placement uses the retained recent candles' high/low range.
// Its bounded samples and extrema advance with the available main head, never
// the viewport. Height and gap remain adjustable in Inputs.
// v1.3 safeguards retained: sample confirmation, missing-data coverage,
// right-edge intrabar ranges, DST-safe overnight anchoring, zoom-aware labels.
// Standard time-based charts only. The default ladder ends at 12M.
// The time ribbon is visible on H1 and lower, independently of optional range layers.
// Use TradingView price-scale menu > Scale price chart only to keep distant
// monthly objectives from squeezing the intraday candles.
// Model1 is explicitly selected and linked to a selected CRT anchor. CISD uses
// only an assigned-timeframe confirmed close strictly beyond its FULL high/low.
// Bias is MANUAL, not a signal: each dropdown recolors that recurring slot.
// Optional selected-date scope leaves all other dates neutral.
// Range highs/lows use available chart-session data. Missing opening data is
// marked PARTIAL. Developing ranges change until their time window finishes.
// On bars crossing a range boundary, 1m/5m intrabars prevent including prices
// from outside that range. Older intrabars can be unavailable on TradingView;
// the chart warns and affected ranges are omitted/marked PARTIAL, not guessed.
// Completed values are frozen. No orders, entry confirmation or edge claims.

// Display repair: daily captions follow the exchange trading day, including overnight sessions.
// Range and DOL prices are unchanged; centered outside markers carry hover details.
// 2026-10-13: simple dated ribbon controls, black range borders, and guarded
// developing monthly-purge display (source close remains explicitly pending).
// BEGIN GENERATED GTOP RULES
// Generated from rules/gtop_rules.json. Do not edit this block.
string GTOP_RULESET_VERSION = "1.3.0"
string GTOP_RULESET_SHA256 = "2a9f4ec9b85b58f1c8103d8782ac4e696cee4277237195578148bc59a0af9980"

// GTOP-EVIDENCE-005; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_chart_contiguous(int expected, int starts, int previous_close, int projected_open) =>
    (((starts == expected)) or (((previous_close == expected)) and ((projected_open == starts)) and ((starts > previous_close))))

// GTOP-RANGE-002; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_inside(float c, float hi, float lo) =>
    ((lo < c) and (c < hi))

// GTOP-RANGE-003; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_outside(float c, float hi, float lo) =>
    (((c > hi)) or ((c < lo)))

// GTOP-RANGE-002; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_at_boundary(float c, float hi, float lo) =>
    (((c == hi)) or ((c == lo)))

// GTOP-RANGE-001; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_purged(float h, float l, float level, bool buy_side) =>
    (buy_side ? ((h > level)) : ((l < level)))

// GTOP-MODEL1-001; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_body_purge(float o, float h, float l, float c, float level, bool buy_side) =>
    (buy_side ? (((o <= level) and (level < c)) or ((l < level) and (level < o) and (o < c))) : (((c < level) and (level <= o)) or ((c < o) and (o < level) and (level < h))))

// GTOP-CISD-001; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_cisd(float c, float model_hi, float model_lo, bool bearish) =>
    (bearish ? ((c < model_lo)) : ((c > model_hi)))

// GTOP-VARIANT-004; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_inside_bar(float h, float l, float hi, float lo) =>
    (((h <= hi)) and ((l >= lo)))

// GTOP-VARIANT-V6-EXCLUSIVE; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_v6_before_full(bool initial_return, bool swept_extreme, bool full_before, bool full_same_bar) =>
    (initial_return and swept_extreme and (not full_before) and (not full_same_bar))

// GTOP-SOUP-001; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_soup_confirmation(float o, float h, float l, float c, float hi, float lo, bool bearish) =>
    (bearish ? (((h > hi)) and ((((lo < c) and (c < hi)) and ((l >= lo))) or (((lo < o) and (o < hi)) and ((c < lo))))) : (((l < lo)) and ((((lo < c) and (c < hi)) and ((h <= hi))) or (((lo < o) and (o < hi)) and ((c > hi))))))

// GTOP-SOUP-003; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_adverse_extension(float h, float l, float hi, float lo, bool bearish) =>
    (bearish ? (((h > hi)) ? (h - hi) : 0.0) : (((l < lo)) ? (lo - l) : 0.0))

// GTOP-SOUP-003; caller establishes confirmed timeframe and coverage.
f_gtop_extension_percent(float points, float hi, float lo) =>
    (((hi > lo)) ? ((100.0 * points) / (hi - lo)) : 0.0)

f_gtop_assigned_tf(string sourceTF) =>
    switch sourceTF
        "1M" => "1D"
        "1W" => "240"
        "1D" => "60"
        "240" => "15"
        "60" => "5"
        => ""
// END GENERATED GTOP RULES

// SETTINGS -------------------------------------------------------------------
// Automatic boxes are selected from price, never a named example date.
string G_QUICK = "Quick display"
string G_DATED_SHIFT = "Color a dated shift"
string G_SHIFT_LEGACY = "Advanced · saved chart-picked shift colors"
string G_RIBBON_ADV = "Advanced ribbon colors | saved three-day annotations"
bool showShifts = input.bool(true, "Time ribbon", inline="ribbonQuick", group=G_QUICK, tooltip="Show or hide the time ribbon on H1 and lower, including its optional H4 row.")
bool autoOn = input.bool(true, "Range boxes", group=G_QUICK, tooltip="Show or hide range drawings and DOL lines only. Evidence, variants, callouts and captures keep their own controls. Personal drawings are unchanged.")
bool watermarkOn = input.bool(true, "Watermark", group=G_QUICK)
bool stickyOn = input.bool(true, "Sticky notes", group=G_QUICK, tooltip="Show or hide your six note rules independently of the watermark, ribbon and ranges. Blank rules draw nothing.")
// maxVisibleRangeBoxes detail: Total visible price-range boxes across automatic active/watch/history, manual anchors, selected Model1, gray context and scheduled ranges. Priority: automatic active/watch current then nearest higher, oldest first; then automatic history, optional manual/Model1/context, then scheduled. Omitted boxes omit their associated lines and labels. Ribbon boxes are separate.
int maxVisibleRangeBoxes = input.int(12, "Maximum visible range boxes", minval=1, maxval=50, group=G_QUICK, tooltip="Total range-box cap. Priority: active/watch (current then higher, oldest first), history, manual/context, scheduled. Omitted boxes also omit their labels/lines. Ribbon is separate.")
string G_AUTO = "Butterfly of Relevance"
// historyOn detail: Off: current relevance follows the latest available confirmed source evidence, independent of panning; actual Bar Replay limits available parent evidence. On: add up to six recent past qualified ranges per current/parent layer and GTOP H4, evaluated at the same latest available head, after objective delivery or source-close invalidation. Unqualified candles stay hidden. A close-proven completed V2 can enter history directly without an active box. The first completed variant stays frozen; later double-purge and return-objective events append to it. History off hides every retired range, including double-purge follow-through. Named variants require closed-candle evidence; ambiguous same-candle order stays unclassified.
bool historyOn = input.bool(false, "History", group=G_AUTO, tooltip="Show retired qualified ranges after delivery/invalidation; off hides them all. First completed variant stays frozen; later double-purge facts append. Closed evidence required; panning does not change status.")
int historyKeep = 24 // Retain enough completed H4 sessions for double-purge follow-through; display remains capped.
// autoScope detail: Default Butterfly context: the current chart source plus the next 3 higher ladder sources, adjustable with Higher timeframe layers. Ladder: 3m, 5m, 15m, H1, H4 (selected source), D1, W1, 1M, 3M, 6M, 12M. Never lower layers. Non-ladder charts start at the nearest higher rung. Current + one higher keeps the compact two-layer view. Qualification still requires a strict purge, own-timeframe close inside and pending DOL. Ordinary history uses current plus one parent and GTOP H4; recent double-purge records may appear on any selected layer.
string autoScope = input.string("Butterfly context", "Automatic layer view", options=["Butterfly context", "Current + one higher", "Manual layers"], group=G_AUTO, tooltip="Butterfly: current source plus 3 higher ladder layers. Compact: current + one higher. No lower layers. Relevant ranges require strict purge, inside source close and pending DOL. History remains opt-in.")
string parentChoice = input.string("Automatic", "Higher layer override", options=["Automatic", "3", "5", "15", "60", "240", "1D", "1W", "1M", "3M", "6M", "12M"], group=G_AUTO, tooltip="Current + one higher only. Minutes: 3=3m, 60=H1, 240=selected H4. Must exceed the chart timeframe; invalid choices show a notice and add no layer.", active=autoScope == "Current + one higher")
bool autoM = input.bool(false, "Monthly", inline="layers", group=G_AUTO, active=autoScope == "Manual layers")
bool autoW = input.bool(false, "Weekly", inline="layers", group=G_AUTO, active=autoScope == "Manual layers")
bool autoD = input.bool(false, "Daily", inline="layers", group=G_AUTO, active=autoScope == "Manual layers")
bool auto3M = input.bool(false, "3M", inline="longLayers", group=G_AUTO, active=autoScope == "Manual layers")
